course: dictionary
lesson: 4353
title: The guitar and the sound of strings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A guitar is a musical instrument with strings. You play it with your fingers or a small pick. Most guitars have 6 strings. In the sentences «play the guitar», «guitar lessons» and «strum the guitar», the word guitar names the thing you play.
explain: Every sound starts with something wobbling very fast. «A short, tight guitar string vibrates fast and sounds high; a long, loose string vibrates slowly and sounds low.» So the length and tightness of a string change how high or low its sound is.
explain: Some guitars need help to be heard. «An electric guitar has a solid body and is quiet until it is plugged into an amplifier.» An acoustic guitar is different: «an acoustic guitar has a hollow body that makes it louder without electricity.»
explain: Learning the guitar takes time. The sentence «Guitar strings hurt» shows that the start is hard for everyone. Sore fingers and wrong notes at first are normal, so keep practising.
fact: A guitar is a musical instrument with strings.
fact: A guitar usually has 6 strings.
fact: You can play a guitar with your fingers or a small pick.
fact: An electric guitar needs an amplifier to sound loud.
fact: A shorter, tighter string makes a higher sound.
exercise: «Play the guitar with your fingers or a small pick.» What is a guitar? | A kitchen tool | *A musical instrument with strings | A kind of drum | A type of bird
exercise: How many strings does a guitar usually have? | 12 | *6 | 10 | 4
exercise: «An electric guitar is quiet until it is plugged into an amplifier.» What does an electric guitar need to sound loud? | *An amplifier | A pick | A longer string | A hollow body
test: Which string makes a higher sound: a short, tight string or a long, loose string? | Both sound exactly the same | *A short, tight string | A long, loose string | Neither makes a sound
test: What makes an acoustic guitar louder without electricity? | A plugged-in amplifier | Its loose strings | Its solid body | *Its hollow body
exam: Which sentence is true about a guitar? | A guitar has no strings at all | A guitar is a kind of bird | *A guitar is a musical instrument with strings | An electric guitar is loud without an amplifier
